<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Terms &amp; Conditions | Trace</title>
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        :root {
            --bg: #090d0b;
            --surface: #101613;
            --surface-secondary: #141b17;
            --border: #26332d;
            --border-strong: #334139;
            --text: #f5f7f6;
            --secondary: #9aa7a0;
            --muted: #6f7c74;
            --accent: #63d39b;
        }

        body {
            min-height: 100vh;
            padding: 32px 20px;
            background: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text);
            font-family: Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
        }

        .page {
            width: min(820px, 100%);
            margin: 0 auto;
        }

        header {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: space-between;
            gap: 16px;
            padding: 8px 0 24px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
        }

        .brand {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 10px;
            color: var(--text);
            font-size: 19px;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-decoration: none;
        }

        .brand-icon {
            width: 36px;
            height: 36px;
            display: grid;
            place-items: center;
            border-radius: 8px;
            background: var(--accent);
            color: #07100b;
            font-size: 16px;
        }

        .back-link {
            color: var(--secondary);
            font-size: 13px;
            text-decoration: none;
        }

        .back-link:hover,
        .brand:hover {
            color: var(--accent);
        }

        main {
            margin-top: 32px;
            padding: 36px clamp(22px, 6vw, 54px);
            border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
            border-radius: 16px;
            background: var(--surface);
        }

        h1 {
            font-size: clamp(30px, 6vw, 40px);
            line-height: 1.15;
        }

        .updated {
            margin-top: 10px;
            color: var(--muted);
            font-size: 13px;
        }

        .intro {
            margin-top: 24px;
            color: var(--secondary);
            line-height: 1.7;
        }

        section {
            margin-top: 28px;
        }

        h2 {
            margin-bottom: 9px;
            color: var(--text);
            font-size: 17px;
        }

        section p,
        section li {
            color: var(--secondary);
            font-size: 14px;
            line-height: 1.75;
        }

        ul {
            margin: 10px 0 0 20px;
        }

        li+li {
            margin-top: 5px;
        }

        footer {
            padding: 22px 0;
            color: var(--muted);
            font-size: 12px;
            text-align: center;
        }

        @media (max-width: 520px) {
            body {
                padding: 20px 14px;
            }

            main {
                margin-top: 20px;
                padding: 28px 20px;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <div class="page">
        <header>
            <a class="brand" href="/">
                <span class="brand-icon">↗</span>
                Trace
            </a>
            <a class="back-link" href="/signup">Back to sign up</a>
        </header>

        <main>
            <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
            <p class="updated">Last updated: October 3, 2026</p>
            <p class="intro">These Terms govern your use of Trace, a service for creating, managing, and measuring
                shortened URLs. By creating an account or using Trace, you agree to these Terms.</p>

            <section>
                <h2>1. Your account</h2>
                <p>Provide accurate account information and keep your login credentials secure. You are responsible for
                    activity performed through your account and should notify us promptly if you suspect unauthorized
                    access.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>2. Short links and destination content</h2>
                <p>You retain responsibility for the URLs you submit, the destination pages they lead to, and how you
                    distribute your short links. You must have the rights and permissions needed to use that content. Do
                    not use Trace to create or share links that:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Facilitate fraud, phishing, malware, or other illegal activity.</li>
                    <li>Infringe another person's rights or distribute harmful or deceptive content.</li>
                    <li>Evade security controls or interfere with the service or its users.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>3. Link analytics</h2>
                <p>Trace may record link visits and related technical information, such as visit timestamps, to provide
                    link statistics and operate the service. Analytics are estimates and may be affected by bots,
                    privacy tools, network conditions, or other factors; they are not guaranteed to be complete or
                    exact.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>4. Acceptable use and enforcement</h2>
                <p>Use Trace lawfully and do not disrupt, overload, probe, or attempt unauthorized access to the
                    service. We may restrict or suspend links or accounts that violate these Terms, create a security
                    risk, or expose Trace or others to legal harm.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>5. Service availability and changes</h2>
                <p>We work to keep Trace available, but the service may change or be interrupted for maintenance,
                    security, or operational reasons. We may update these Terms as the service evolves. Continued use
                    after updated Terms take effect means you accept the revised Terms.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>6. Disclaimers and liability</h2>
                <p>To the extent permitted by law, Trace is provided as available without warranties that every short
                    link, destination, or analytics result will be uninterrupted, error-free, or suitable for a
                    particular purpose. To the extent permitted by law, Trace is not liable for indirect or
                    consequential losses arising from your use of the service. Nothing in these Terms limits liability
                    that cannot legally be limited.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2>7. Contact</h2>
                <p>For questions about these Terms, use the contact channel provided by the Trace service operator.</p>
            </section>
        </main>

        <footer>© 2026 Trace. Built for the web.</footer>
    </div>
</body>

</html>